# QR-360° viewer sync (building-map-explorer)

## Source of truth

`C:\Users\Robert\Projects\QR-360°-Inspections\QR-360°-Inspections`

New builds are named like `QR-360°_viewer_v1.1.3.html`.

## Linked locations in this repo

| Purpose | Path |
|---------|------|
| Versioned archive | `qr360-viewer/QR-360°_viewer_v*.html` |
| Live iframe target | `public/insp360/viewer.html` |
| App URL builder | `src/lib/insp360Viewer.ts` → `insp360/viewer.html` |

The main program must keep using **`insp360/viewer.html`** (stable). Never point the iframe at a versioned filename.

## When the user ships a new viewer version

1. Confirm the new HTML exists in the Inspections source folder.
2. Run from `building-map-explorer`:

```powershell
npm run sync:qr360-viewer
```

3. That **replaces** older files in `qr360-viewer/` and overwrites `public/insp360/viewer.html`.
4. Tell the user to hard-refresh BME / reopen the gate sphere.

Do not hand-edit `public/insp360/viewer.html` — edit the Inspections source, then sync.
